From a1e758a4f5c1cd34dd6344219bce603dfd446730 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WWE13 Recomp <wwe13-recomp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:48:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 126/126] vulkan: fewer and smaller render passes for
 tile-based GPUs

On Apple GPUs (MoltenVK) every render pass loads and stores its attachments,
and the emulated render targets are up to 4688 rows tall.

- Shared memory uploads that no draw in the current submission has touched are
  recorded into a prelude that is prepended to the submission, instead of
  ending the render pass for a copy in the middle of it. The prelude is fenced
  by barriers at its start and end. Readback copies and Use() mark the pages
  they touch, so a later upload to them still goes in place.
  WWE13_UPLOAD_PRELUDE=0 turns this off.
- Each render pass's render area is trimmed to the union of the scissors and
  clear rectangles used in it (patched into the deferred begin command when the
  pass ends). WWE13_RENDER_AREA_TRIM=0 turns this off.

On the Mac attract mode this cut render encoders from 73.9k to 49.8k and copy
encoders from 60.7k to 8.8k, and passes keep about 65% of the full area. On an
iPad mini (A20 Pro) a WWE '13 entrance at 720p with 2x MSAA holds 29 fps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
